index c6216fb..11f4a49 100644
--- a/agents/IMPLEMENTATION.md
+++ b/agents/IMPLEMENTATION.md
@@ -21,3 +21,11 @@ For detailed change history, use git history and PRs instead of expanding this f
 ### Rosetta workspace documentation: done, 2026-10-21
 
 - Added `docs/CONTEXT.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/ASSUMPTIONS.md`, `docs/TODO.md`, `agents/IMPLEMENTATION.md` and `agents/MEMORY.md`, alongside the Phase 3 `docs/TECHSTACK.md`, `docs/CODEMAP.md` and `docs/DEPENDENCIES.md`. The human docs were left untouched.
+
+### Minimum age (age-restricted products): done, 2026-11-02
+
+- Diverges from the 3.23 release pin: `schema-main.graphql` was regenerated from the local core (3.24 + minimum age, `fetch-local-schema`), not from the release. Generated `src/graphql/*.generated.ts` come from `pnpm run generate`.
+- All new selections carry `@lockSchema(schema: "main")` (`Product.minimumAge` via fragments, `Shop.timeZone`/`minimumAge`, `User.dateOfBirth`/`ageEligible`/`events`) so staging documents keep compiling. `User.isSuperuser` is on the user fragment.
+- `dateOfBirth`, audit `events` and `ageEligible` are read only by the dedicated `CustomerAuditedDetails` query (field-level `@include`, `$isSuperuser`/`$includeAgeEligible`), sent imperatively with `no-cache` at most once per customer per page mount (`useCustomerAuditedDetails`); the main `CustomerDetails` query never selects them. Only superusers see or send the birthday; others see read-only "Meets shop minimum age".
+- UI: product "Minimum age" field and "Age" datagrid column (`src/products`), customer birthday + audit card (`src/customers`), "Age restriction" site settings card (`src/siteSettings`), age error messages for draft finalize and order confirm (`src/utils/errors`).
+- `locale/defaultMessages.json` regenerated with `pnpm run extract-messages`. Changeset: `.changeset/min-age.md` (patch).
